      uvcHighlight4: "Extracted codes surfaced in a high-contrast hero banner with dedicated 1-click clipboard copying.",
      uvcSec1Title: "The Problem with Legacy Services: Date Traps and Token Blindness",
      uvcSec1P1: "Most disposable temporary email services rely on naive regex patterns looking for any sequence of 4 to 6 digits. This architectural flaw produces catastrophic failures: when an incoming message includes the current year \"2026\", a postal code, or a timestamp, the parser erroneously captures the date instead of the genuine OTP.",
      uvcSec1P2: "Furthermore, leading platforms such as Google, Steam, and Discord employ sophisticated token formats like \"G-849201\" or mixed alphanumeric pins. Legacy services fail completely to recognize these tokens, forcing users to sift through raw, unstyled HTML code.",
      uvcSec2Title: "Our Dual-Layer Edge Engine: 100% Extraction Accuracy",
      uvcSec2P1: "Our engineering team built an advanced edge verification pipeline running across Cloudflare globally distributed datacenters:",
      uvcSec2P2: "1. Semantic Context Analyzer: Evaluates proximity to authentication keywords across 22 languages (e.g., verification code, OTP, رمز التحقق, code de confirmation) and scores tokens mathematically.",
      uvcSec2P3: "2. Link Dissector: Parses complex CTA buttons generated by SendGrid, Mailgun, and Amazon SES, stripping redirect telemetry to enable clean, direct 1-click activations.",
      uvcCompRow1Feat: "Google G-XXXXXX Token Support",
      uvcCompRow1Legacy: "Total failure (ignores token prefix)",
      uvcCompRow1Our: "Native support with instant extraction",
      uvcCompRow2Feat: "Immunity to Date Traps (e.g., 2026)",
      uvcCompRow2Legacy: "Displays the year as OTP by mistake",
      uvcCompRow2Our: "Smart contextual validation filtering",
      uvcCompRow3Feat: "Alphanumeric & Steam Guard Codes",
      uvcCompRow3Legacy: "Unsupported (numeric only)",
      uvcCompRow3Our: "Full alphanumeric regex coverage",
      uvcCompRow4Feat: "Masked CTA Activation Buttons",
      uvcCompRow4Legacy: "Lost inside unformatted HTML",
      uvcCompRow4Our: "Extracted to dedicated panel for copying",
      uvcFaq1Q: "Why do legacy temporary mail platforms fail on Google security emails?",
      uvcFaq1A: "Because Google prepends the letter \"G-\" to verification passcodes. Naive numeric parsers treat the hyphen as punctuation and ignore or truncate the authentic token.",
      uvcFaq2Q: "Does your engine click verification links automatically?",
      uvcFaq2A: "No. Automated pre-fetching would prematurely invalidate single-use security links. We extract the URL safely and let you click or copy it intentionally.",
      uvcFaq3Q: "Are non-English verification emails supported?",
      uvcFaq3A: "Yes. Our semantic analyzer recognizes verification keywords across all 22 supported languages on the platform.",
      wsBadge: "Next-Gen Infrastructure",
      wsSubtitle: "An architectural exploration of Cloudflare Durable Objects and WebSocket Hibernation pushing emails to your browser live with zero battery drain or page reloads.",
      wsHighlight1: "Sub-300ms message push to your screen the millisecond an email hits our edge nodes.",
      wsHighlight2: "Zero page reloads required, creating a seamless, lightning-fast application experience.",
      wsHighlight3: "Negligible data and battery consumption via edge-level WebSocket hibernation.",
      wsHighlight4: "Automatic seamless reconnection when switching between Wi-Fi and mobile networks.",
      wsSec1Title: "The Flaw of Polling in Legacy Temporary Inboxes",
      wsSec1P1: "Most disposable email websites rely on periodic HTTP long-polling, firing requests every 5 seconds to query for new messages. This archaic approach drains device battery, wastes cellular data, and introduces delays of 5 to 15 seconds.",
      wsSec1P2: "If you leave the tab backgrounded, rate limits or browser throttling often pause polling entirely, leaving you waiting indefinitely for an activation code that already arrived.",
      wsSec2Title: "The Solution: Edge-Native WebSockets and Hibernation",
      wsSec2P1: "We engineered our mailboxes directly on Cloudflare Durable Objects. When you load the application, your browser establishes a secure, persistent WebSocket connection to your isolated container.",
      wsSec2P2: "When an email arrives, Cloudflare Email Routing parses it in-memory and pushes the sanitized payload through the open WebSocket socket directly into your inbox list in under 300 milliseconds.",
      wsCompRow1Feat: "Message Delivery Latency",
