      mlHighlight3: "Direct link extraction surfaces the target destination cleanly with one-click copy capability.",
      mlHighlight4: "Fully compatible with modern passwordless stacks including Supabase, Auth0, and Firebase.",
      mlSec1Title: "The Dilemma: Why Magic Links Expire Prematurely on Other Services",
      mlSec1P1: "Passwordless authentication relies on single-use encrypted URLs. When an authentication provider sends a magic link, legacy temporary email platforms often run automated link scanners that fire preview requests against every link in the email.",
      mlSec1P2: "The moment an automated crawler touches a single-use URL, the token is consumed. When the human user clicks the link moments later, they are greeted by a frustrating error: \"This magic link has already been used or expired.\"",
      mlSec2Title: "How Our Passive Ingestion Engine Protects Your Tokens",
      mlSec2P1: "We engineered our mail parser to be completely passive. We inspect inbound HTML payloads without executing network requests or pre-fetching external endpoints.",
      mlSec2P2: "The verified link is extracted, stripped of unnecessary redirect parameters, and delivered straight to your screen, ensuring that you—and only you—initiate the single-use authentication request.",
